      "context": "We share a screen (the browser's picker, our own tab left out). A compact red pill in the top-left corner, beside the encryption badge and as tall as it, says so — “Sharing screen”, a sound glyph when the tab or system gave sound — with Stop inside. It stays when the controls fade over their screen. A “Your screen” tile top right shows what goes out (contained on black); Share is white (on). The browser's own “Stop sharing” bar, or the shared window closing, ends it with a notice.",
